  "notes": "The *other* Stockholm camp — Murlyn Studios, R&B-leaning Swedish pop for American vocal groups: 71–128 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and ballads at 71–98. The one place `humanize` moves is stated outright — \"R&B-informed programmed kit with **live-feel velocity variation**\" — so `velocityVar` runs at 0.22 against a still-tight grid, which is the highest velocity spread on the Stockholm bench. Three placement facts are quoted: \"kick 1/3 plus the '&' of 4\", \"snare 2&4 with a 16th ghost before beat 4\" (the ghost on \"3a\" at 0.3 — on the e/&/a grid `engine/src/generators/grid.rs` parses, the 16th before beat 4 is \"3a\"; \"4e\" falls after it), and \"16th shaker\". The bass is a fretless imitation — \"legato synth bass with slides between roots\" — which is `independent_riff` at 0.8 with `glideProb` 0.35, the highest in this batch, and it is the clearest separation from the 98 Degrees artist model that shares these records. Harmony is I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V \"with a ii–V push into the chorus\" over flat-key majors and two named minors, so `keys` is authored. The arrangement writes \"four-part close harmony… into the arrangement\" with \"the last line doubled an octave up\", which is the octave-echo counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it medium-high. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 92.",
